    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <description><![CDATA[The HashCheck Shell Extension makes it easy for anyone to calculate and verify checksums and hashes from Windows Explorer. In addition to integrating file checksumming functionality into Windows, HashCheck can also create and verify SFV files (and other forms of checksum files, such as .md5 files). It is fast and efficient, with a very light disk and memory footprint, and it is open-source.
]]></description>
    <summary>The HashCheck Shell Extension makes it easy for anyone to calculate and verify checksums and hashes from Windows Explorer.</summary>
    <releaseNotes><![CDATA[[Releases](https://github.com/idrassi/HashCheck/releases)

## HashCheck 2.6.3

HashCheck 2.6.3 adds separate checksum file creation and makes verification results easier to review. It also fixes installation issues and restores checksum file opening on Wine 9.0.

### Fixed Issues

- Fixed Windows PowerShell module lookup when the installer is launched from PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`). The same correction applies during uninstall. Fixes #43.
- Fixed opening checksum files on Wine 9.0, which stopped working in version 2.6.0. Fixes #41.
- Fixed WinGet identification of this fork as `idrassi.HashCheckShellExtension`. Fixes https://github.com/idrassi/DirHash/issues/39.
- Checksum loading errors now include the underlying cause. Verification stops if there isn't enough memory to load every entry, preventing incomplete results from being shown. Large checksum files still require substantial memory. Relates to #28.

### Other Changes

- Added **Create Separate Checksum Files...** to Explorer's context menus, including the Windows 11 menu. This creates a checksum file beside each input file, with options for the hash type and handling existing output files. It's also available through `HashCheckPackageHost.exe /create /separate`. Fixes #8.
- The verification window can now be resized or maximized and remembers its size and position. A new **Copy...** menu supports copying all results or just the summary; **Ctrl+C** copies selected rows. Relates to #42.
- Added colors to the verification summary. The match count turns green only when every listed file matches. Mismatches appear in red and unreadable files in yellow, while high contrast mode keeps system colors. Fixes #39.
- Added an initial check that can flag missing or unreadable files before hashing starts. This check has a time limit so unavailable network paths don't keep it waiting indefinitely. Relates to #38.
- Updated the application icons and added a dedicated installer icon. Thanks to @xmha97 for #45.


## Merged PRs
* Improve icons by @xmha97 in https://github.com/idrassi/HashCheck/pull/45

## New Contributors
* @xmha97 made their first contribution in https://github.com/idrassi/HashCheck/pull/45

**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/idrassi/HashCheck/compare/v2.6.2...v2.6.3]]></releaseNotes>
